        "text": "Now the inventory table says:\n- assist.ts: 3 处 (memory recall injections)\n- settled.ts: 1 处 (round settle related)\n- partner-context.ts: 11 处\n- injection-guard.ts: 3 处\n\nHmm, but assist.ts only has recallContext (an injection producer) and taskMemoryBlock. Hmm, \"3 处\" might be approximate/measured differently (e.g., counting lines). Let me check what's in assist.ts historically — maybe there were 3 injection points before refactor. Let me git log assist.ts.\n\nActually, the important thing: the task requires taking over *all remaining injections*. The \"hard standard\" is byte-identical content and position. I need to decide a concrete design that:\n1. Adds providers for lifecycle's 6 sections (persona, verification_iron_law, clarify_contract, current_project, skills, topics)\n2. Takes over the 5 extra.push in lifecycle\n3. Deals with assist.ts's recallContext / taskMemoryBlock (where are they injected? recallContext → lifecycle extra.push #1; taskMemoryBlock → openai-compat instructions tail)\n4. partner-context's 11 segments (contract, goal, discipline blocks, status, guard)\n5. settled.ts 1 处 — settled.ts has no text injection... unless \"1 处\" refers to ingestTurn? Hmm.\n\nWait. Maybe the intended interpretation: these counts in the plan are a rough inventory of \"places that assemble prompt text\", and batch 27's task book inherits them. The task book says \"2.1 assist.ts 的记忆召回注入（3 处）接管\" — but in current code there's only 1 recall injection in assist usage. Let me check git history whether assist.ts used to have 3 injections.\n\nLet me grep for \"记忆\" injections elsewhere: maybe in session.ts or group-runtime.ts there are additional injections. Let's check all places that call `memoryEngine.buildContext` or push system messages with memory."
