      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now, let's think about \"settled.ts 1 处\". There's really nothing there. Unless they mean the memory ingest writes... no. I'll report: settled.ts 现无提示词注入（只有记忆写入/导出/观察层），故无可接管；已在变更记录与回复中说明。 But the task explicitly asks to take it over. I must not invent an injection. I'll document.\n\nSimilarly \"assist.ts 3 处\": recallContext is used in lifecycle (1). taskMemoryBlock in openai-compat (1). That's 2 injection producers. What's the third? Maybe `PERSONA`/`WORKER_PERSONA`? They're text constants used by lifecycle's persona section. Could count as \"assist 的记忆/人格注入 3 处\": recallContext, taskMemoryBlock, PERSONA/WORKER_PERSONA? Hmm.\n\nLet me grep assist exports usage: memoryEngine, scopeOf, preferenceScopeOf, recallContext, taskMemoryBlock, skillStore, PERSONA, WORKER_PERSONA, CHANCELLOR_ENABLED, seedChiefPartner, workerChatEnabled.\n\nAn honest inventory to report:\n- assist.ts: 2 注入产出口 — `recallContext`（lifecycle beforeRequest 第 1 处 extra.push）与 `taskMemoryBlock`（openai-compat 任务 instructions 尾部）。\n- settled.ts: 0 注入（只有记忆写入/导出/观察层）。\n- partner-context.ts: 12 段（契约/目标/纪律 7~8 段/在办/防线），实际拼成 1 个 text。\n\nWait, but the task says \"partner-context.ts 11 段\". Let me count more carefully what \"段\" means: buildPartnerTurnContext's `text` = [contract, goal, discipline, status, guard]. Discipline = [verificationIronLaw, RULING, WORK_SILENCE, GROUNDING, ARTIFACT_HANDOFF, OWNER_DATA, BRIEF_CARD, ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION] = 8. So total distinguishable segments = 4 + 8 = 12 (chief: 11). So \"11 段\" ≈ chief (验证铁律 absent for chief? `verificationIronLawFor(chief)` returns undefined presumably since lifecycle owns it) → chief has 7 discipline blocks + 4 = 11. Yes! For chief: verificationIronLawFor returns undefined (lifecycle owns), brief card skipped → 8-2 = 6 discipline + contract/goal/status/guard = 10... hmm.\n\nActually verificationIronLawFor chief → undefined, brief card chief → undefined: 8-2=6 discipline. 6+4 = 10. If contract exists... Still \"11\" is fuzzy.\n\nI'll take over partner-context by splitting its 5 top-level parts into providers, and the discipline's individual blocks into providers too (so dedupe can act on e.g. verification_iron_law if lifecycle also injects it — which is exactly the \"重复\" to discover). That's where the framework's value shows: `verification_iron_law` is injected by lifecycle for chief and skipped in partner-context for chief (they already avoid duplication). Also INJECTION_GUARD is injected by lifecycle section for chief AND by partner-context guard for partners — mutually exclusive by identity, not duplicate.\n\nReal potential duplicates after takeover:\n- `injection_guard` (lifecycle section for chief) vs partner-context guard (for partners) — same id, same text, but never both present... unless a chief partner session: partnerId = \"chief\" → partner-context guard IS injected (buildPartnerTurnContext is called for any partnerId including chief). Wait: lifecycle injects partner turn context for any partnerId (including chief!). And lifecycle's `injection_guard` section in system also appears for chief. So for the chief partner session, INJECTION_GUARD is injected twice: once as system section, once at the tail of partner turn context message! That's a genuine duplicate I can discover by giving both entries the same id `injection_guard` with different channels... but dedupe is per-id globally, which would delete one of them → changing content! Careful: dedupe is across channels? `collectInjections` dedupes across the whole array then splits by channel; so same id in both channels → one survives. That would change behavior (removing a duplicate).\n\nHmm, the task says: \"全量接管后可能出现同 id 重复（例如两处都注入了纪律段）——这正是框架的价值：发现重复就合并成一条，并在变更记录里列出哪几处原来重复了\". So we're *allowed/expected* to dedupe, which changes bytes (removes a duplicate). But hard standard says byte-identical... Contradiction resolved by: byte-identical per-site *except* where duplicates are found, which are then merged and documented. The task explicitly asks to list duplicates in the change record. So dedupe removing true duplicates is intended behavior change.\n\nBut careful: dedupe across channels could remove a system section and keep a message entry, which changes position/content structure. Safer: dedupe within channel. And for the chief injection_guard duplication (system vs message), merging is risky. Let me check whether chief partner sessions actually get both.\n\nIn lifecycle, `buildPartnerTurnContext` is called when `partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession(api.conversationId)` is truthy. For the chief's main conversation, is there a session link? `ensureChiefPartner` seeds a chief partner; is the main conversation linked to it? Let me check partners.ts sessionIdOfPartner and partnerIdOfSession for chief. The partner-context comment says \"**总管（chief）的验证铁律由 lifecycle 的 persona 段注入**，这里跳过\" — implying partner-context IS used for chief. And `guard` is injected for chief too. So yes: for the chief's linked session, INJECTION_GUARD appears in system (section) and in message (partner context tail). That's a real duplicate — worth reporting.\n\nShould I merge it? Removing the guard from partner context for chief would change bytes. The task says duplicates should be merged. But \"逐字节一致是硬标准\" per site. I think the right move: **detect and report** duplicates, and only merge when it doesn't change semantics? The task says \"发现重复就合并成一条\". Hmm.\n\nGiven the tension, I'll implement dedupe within the framework (already exists) but *per channel*, and in the actual collection I'll keep sites independent (each render collects one provider), so no cross-site dedupe happens at runtime except where I deliberately collect multiple. Then how do duplicates get merged? \n\nHmm. Maybe better: lifecycle's beforeRequest collects ALL message-channel injections at once (memory, slash, recover, turnLimit, partner-context). Within that collection, give partner-context sub-entries ids like `partner:verification_iron_law` etc. The guard entry from partner-context has id `injection_guard` (same as section) — but it's in the message channel. If I dedupe only within channel, no merge. If across channels, merge would drop the message copy (keeping system) → content change (removing a duplicate) which is arguably intended.\n\nRisk: dropping the guard from partner tail for chief changes byte content and the \"position\". I don't want to silently change behavior. But the task explicitly wants duplicates listed, not necessarily removed at runtime? \"发现重复就合并成一条，并在变更记录里列出'哪几处原来重复了'\" — merge AND list.\n\nHmm. Which duplicates are safe to merge?\n1. Chief's injection_guard system + message tail. Removing the message copy is safe content-wise (same text). But it changes tokens. Since the task's whole premise is dedupe value, I'll do it: partner-context guard provider returns the entry, and in the combined message collection I'll dedupe against system-collected ids? That requires cross-channel awareness in lifecycle's collection: collect system providers + message providers in one call, then dedupe, then split. That's what collectInjections does globally. So if I collect all at once, dedupe across channels works as designed.\n\nBut collectInjections is called per render for sections (each section separately) — so the section guard and the message guard are collected in different calls → no dedupe. To actually dedupe, I'd need a single collection pass for the whole request, which doesn't fit \"each section renders itself\".\n\nSo realistically, the framework can only dedupe *within a single collection call*. Since sections render independently, cross-section duplicates can't be deduped without restructuring durable section rendering (not worth it; would change section keys).\n\nTherefore: implement dedupe where collections are combined (message channel: all 5 extra.push in one call; partner-context's internal segments in one call). Report cross-channel duplicates found (chief guard) as *observed but not merged* — because merging would require a cross-channel collection pass that durable sections can't participate in. Hmm, but that's a weak outcome vs the task.\n\nAlternatively, I can drop the guard in `buildPartnerTurnContext` when partnerId === CHIEF (mirroring the verification-law skip) — that's a behavior change but removes a real duplicate, and it's exactly the kind of cleanup the task wants. But \"逐字节一致\" per site would fail for chief guard. The task's §5.1 explicitly authorizes merging duplicates. I'll do it? Risky: other tests (partner-context.test) may assert guard presence for chief. Let me check partner-context.test.ts."
      }
