      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Chief's main conversation: does the chief partner get linked to the main conversation? `ensureChiefPartner` maybe only creates the partner record; the main conversation (partnerIdOfSession=null) is \"master conversation\" and D15 says chief continues to read global. The comment in partner-context says chief's verification is injected by lifecycle, and buildPartnerTurnContext for chiefId is used in tests with a linked session 607. In production, is a session ever linked to chief? Possibly if the chief has its own conversation (side panel). Then both persona section (chief SOUL) and partner-context fire for that chief session → duplicate guard and possibly duplicate persona-ish content? Persona section injects resolvePersona (chief SOUL), partner context injects discipline (no SOUL in text). So for a chief-linked session: guard twice.\n\nI'll report this as a duplicate found (same id `injection_guard`, system + message). Do I merge? Merging across channels requires a combined collection. I could simply drop the partner-context guard for `partnerId === CHIEF_PARTNER_ID` — because lifecycle's section already injects it for chief sessions (guard section is not gated by identity!). Check: lifecycle `injection_guard` section render has no identity check → applies to ALL sessions including partner sessions. So for any partner session, guard IS injected as a system section *and* again via partner-context. Wait — that means every partner session gets the guard twice already, not just chief! Indeed the section has no gate. And partner-context adds `guard` for every partner turn.\n\nSo this is a genuine global duplicate: `injection_guard` in lifecycle section (all sessions) + partner-context tail (all partner sessions). That's exactly the \"同 id 重复\" the task expects us to find! \n\nMerging: remove partner-context's guard entirely (keep lifecycle's section). Behavior change: partner sessions lose the tail copy but still see the section copy earlier. Content set changes (one copy instead of two). The task explicitly sanctions merging duplicates and listing them. But is the position/content \"byte-identical\"? For that site no — but the task's §5.1 overrides for duplicates.\n\nHmm, risk: partner session's system sections — is `persona` section undefined for non-chief partners, and guard still present? Yes, guard independent. So partner sessions do have the section (system). Removing the tail copy is safe in terms of \"model still sees the discipline once\", and reduces tokens.\n\nBut wait: is the guard section's text identical to partner-context's? Both `INJECTION_GUARD`. Yes, same constant.\n\nHowever, does the partner-context guard sit in a *message* appended at the very end of the request, making it more salient/recency-effective? Removing it changes prompt semantics slightly. The task wants dedupe. I'll do it but explicitly document as the one intentional content change (duplicate merged), and keep a rollback? Adding a switch would be over-engineering. Hmm, \"新能力给回滚开关\" applies to new capabilities. This is a dedupe; no switch needed since removing a duplicate is the point.\n\nHmm, but \"逐字节一致是硬标准\" — a reviewer might consider removing the guard a violation. The task's §5.1 says \"发现重复就合并成一条，并在变更记录里列出\". I'll implement the merge ONLY for this duplicate, with a test asserting partner turn text no longer carries the tail guard while the system section still does. And keep `buildPartnerTurnContext().guard` field? Tests assert `context.guard` matches 【材料安全】 and `text = discipline + \\n\\n + guard`. If I remove it, those tests change. That's invasive. Maybe better: keep the field but mark? No.\n\nAlternative: don't remove; just report. The task's phrasing \"发现重复就合并成一条\" is an expectation, and “这正是框架的价值”. If I don't merge, I've done B/C/D takeover but skipped the dedupe demonstration. Risk of failing requirement 5.1.\n\nCompromise: merge at the *collection* level within partner-context (no internal dup), and for the cross-channel guard, apply dedupe in lifecycle by collecting the section guard and the partner context together? Not possible since sections render separately... BUT: I can make lifecycle's beforeRequest *not* inject the partner guard, i.e., remove it from `buildPartnerTurnContext` — same thing.\n\nDecision: merge by removing partner-context's guard copy, updating its tests, documenting. Actually wait — there's a subtlety: `buildPartnerTurnContext` is also used by `group-runtime.buildMemberInput`. Do group member sessions get the lifecycle section? They use the same harness/extension, so yes, the guard section applies. So removal is consistent everywhere.\n\nHmm, one more consideration: `persona` section returns undefined for non-chief partners, but `injection_guard` section doesn't. Right.\n\nLet me look at group-runtime to confirm it goes through the same lifecycle extension."
      }
    ],
