        "text": "Good template for order snapshot test.\n\nNow let me plan the implementation concretely and write code. This is a large but mechanical change. Let me be careful with imports to avoid cycles:\n\n- `injection.ts` currently imports injection-guard only. I'll add `InjectionContext` fields + order constants + `auditInjections(registry, ctx)`.\n- New `agent/lifecycle-injections.ts`: providers for persona / verification / clarify / current_project / skills / topics. Imports: `./injection.ts` (types), `../partners.ts`, `../projects.ts`? currentProject is in `./shared.ts`, `../topics.ts`, `./turn-gate.ts`, `../delegation.ts`, `./assist.ts` (PERSONA/WORKER_PERSONA/skillStore), `./injection-guard.ts` (wrapUntrustedObjective), `@earendil-works/pi-durable`? no.\n  Cycle check: assist.ts imports injection.ts? If assist exports memory providers, it imports injection.ts. injection.ts doesn't import assist. lifecycle-injections imports assist → fine (assist doesn't import lifecycle-injections).\n- `assist.ts`: add `memoryProvider`, `taskMemoryProvider` (imports injection.ts types). assist currently imports many modules; adding injection.ts is fine (injection.ts imports injection-guard only, which imports nothing local).\n- `partner-context.ts`: add providers + registry list. Imports injection.ts. Note partner-context imports turn-gate, delegation, partners. Fine.\n- New `agent/injection-registry.ts`: imports all providers from the three modules + injection.ts, exports `INJECTION_REGISTRY`. index.ts imports it for audit. lifecycle imports it? lifecycle needs individual providers, not the registry. But to guarantee \"registry is the source of truth\", lifecycle could import providers from the same modules — fine.\n\nWait, potential cycle: injection-registry.ts imports lifecycle-injections.ts → imports assist.ts → imports partners/diary/memory... None import registry. index.ts imports registry. No cycle.\n\nBut careful: lifecycle.ts imports these provider modules, which import lifecycle? No.\n\nNow, `auditInjections` currently loops `INJECTION_REGISTRY` internally. I'll change signature to `auditInjections(registry, ctx)`. Update injection.test.ts and index.ts.\n\nAlso `INJECTION_REGISTRY` in injection.ts must go (moved). Batch A test asserts length 1 — I'll rewrite tests for B/C/D.\n\n### Context resolution in lifecycle renders\n\nDefine in lifecycle-injections.ts:\n```ts\nexport function partnerOf(conversationId: number): string | null {\n  if (!COMPANIONS_ENABLED) return null;\n  try { return partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession(conversationId); } catch { return null; }\n}\nexport function partnerBlockedAsPartner(partnerId: string | null): boolean // non-chief partner\n```\n\nHmm, but original persona treats `catch` as chief; partnerOf returning null on error matches.\n\nFor topics, group check: `partnersStore().isGroupSession(conversationId)` inside try; on error → chief path. So `isGroupChat(conversationId)` helper with try/catch → false.\n\nFor each render, I'll write minimal code that mirrors the original. Let me write the actual provider implementations:\n\n```ts\n// injection.ts additions\nexport const INJECTION_ORDER = {\n  // B: system sections\n  persona: 0,\n  verification_iron_law: 10,\n  clarify_contract: 20,\n  injection_guard: 30,\n  current_project: 40,\n  skills: 50,\n  topics: 60,\n  // C/D: message channel\n  memory_recall: 100,\n  skill_slash: 110,\n  recover_note: 120,\n  turn_limit: 130,\n  partner_context: 140,\n  // partner-context 内部段（同一 collection 内排序）\n  partner_contract: 200, partner_goal: 210, partner_verification: 220, partner_ruling: 230, partner_work_silence: 240, partner_grounding: 250, partner_artifact_handoff: 260, partner_owner_data: 270, partner_brief_card: 280, partner_attention: 290, partner_status: 300,\n} as const;\n```\nHmm, guard currently order 0. Keep it 30? Order only affects framework sorting within a call. For audit order no. Change guard order to 30 is fine (no cross-call effect). But byte-identical unaffected. Actually to minimize churn, keep guard 0? The order snapshot test would reflect it. Let me set guard = 30 to reflect section order. Fine.\n\nWait, the section physical order is persona, verification, clarify, guard, current_project, skills, topics. Order constants should match that: 0,10,20,30,40,50,60.\n\n### Byte identity tests\n\nFor each section provider, test:\n- persona: with COMPANIONS_ENABLED=false and no DB? The provider uses partnersStore() only if COMPANIONS_ENABLED. In tests, COMPANIONS_ENABLED is env-driven constant evaluated at import (assist.ts? partners.ts). Let me check how COMPANIONS_ENABLED is defined — likely `process.env.COMPANIONS_ENABLED !== \"false\"` default true. Tests set env before importing modules (tool-schema-guard does dynamic import). For injection tests, I can import providers and test with ctx {chatKind:\"chief\"} → `resolvePersona(partnersStore, PERSONA)`. In test env, partnersStore may open real .data? That violates test discipline (\"不碰真实 .data/\"). Hmm. `partnersStore()` likely uses `.data/partners.sqlite`. Need to check."
      }
