      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Set TOPICS_STATE_PATH to temp too.\n\nNow — big question — how much to restructure. Time to write code. Plan of files:\n\n1. `agent/injection.ts`:\n   - extend InjectionContext (chatKind, partnerId, group, userText, turn, dryRun).\n   - add INJECTION_ORDER.\n   - move registry out: change auditInjections signature.\n   - keep guardProvider with order INJECTION_ORDER.injection_guard.\n\n2. `agent/lifecycle-injections.ts` (new): 6 providers + helpers + `LIFECYCLE_SECTION_PROVIDERS` map.\n\n3. `agent/assist.ts`: add `memoryRecallProvider` + `taskMemoryProvider` (using recallContext/taskMemoryBlock) and export.\n\n4. `agent/partner-context.ts`: 12 providers + `PARTNER_CONTEXT_PROVIDERS`; rewrite buildPartnerDisciplineSection/buildPartnerTurnContext to assemble via collectInjections.\n\n5. `agent/injection-registry.ts` (new): `INJECTION_REGISTRY` listing all sources (source: lifecycle/assist/partner-context/settled?). settled has none.\n\n6. `agent/lifecycle.ts`: sections' renders delegate; beforeRequest collects 5 message injections in one collect and pushes in order; positions preserved.\n\n7. `index.ts`: audit uses registry (pass registry).\n\n8. `http-probe.ts`: update expectations.\n\n9. tests: extend injection.test.ts (or new `injection-bcd.test.ts`) with per-site byte-identity + order snapshot; update partner-context tests if guard removed; update batch A assertions.\n\nDecision on guard dedupe: Let me reconsider once more. Removing partner-context guard changes many tests and prompt behavior. The hard standard is emphasized twice (\"硬标准\" in title and 铁律 #4). §5.1 says duplicates may appear and should be merged. A conservative, defensible implementation: keep both (byte-identical), but implement dedupe in the framework and *report* the duplicate; merge only where the same collection contains it. Hmm, that means no actual merge.\n\nWait — maybe there's a better dedupe target that's *within* a single collection: within partner-context, `verificationIronLawFor(partnerId)` and lifecycle's law are different channels/collections. Within lifecycle's beforeRequest collection, are there duplicates? memory vs partner context? No.\n\nSo the only real duplicate is the guard (system + message), and possibly `persona` (system) vs partner-context soul (instructions - not injected in text). Hmm, also `verification_iron_law`: lifecycle injects for chief sessions only; partner context injects for non-chief. For chief partner session: lifecycle injects law (partnerId === chief → lifecycleOwnsVerification true) and partner context's `verificationIronLawFor(chief)` → undefined. No dup.\n\nSo the guard is the one. I think the task expects exactly this discovery: \"例如两处都注入了纪律段\" — they anticipated duplicates. Actually maybe they anticipate `verification_iron_law` duplication, but code already guards it. The guard duplication is real and they may not know.\n\nI'll implement the *merge* for the guard because that's the explicit instruction (\"发现重复就合并成一条\"), and document it clearly as the single intentional behavior change with before/after evidence. I'll update the affected tests to assert the new behavior (tail guard removed, system section still there).\n\nHmm, but wait: is the section guard actually applied to partner sessions? `sections` on the extension apply to every conversation using that extension, including partner sessions. Yes.\n\nBut careful: partner sessions might use a different extension? Let me grep partner-runtime for extension installation."
      }
