        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Good: `PromptSection` type is importable. I can hoist the sections array with type `readonly PromptSection[]` (default Tool generic). Define in lifecycle.ts:\n\n```ts\nexport const LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS: readonly PromptSection[] = [ ... ];\n```\nand use `sections: LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS` in defineExtension. Type compatibility: defineExtension<Tool> extension sections expects `readonly PromptSection<Tool>[]` with Tool=ToolRegistration default → PromptSection[] matches. \n\nThen a test can call `LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS[i].render(fakeInput, fakeContext)` — render's second arg `context: Context`. We can pass `CTX`? Context type is chord's; runtime unused. Pass `undefined as never` maybe. But render uses `input.read.snapshot(...)` and `input.conversationId`. Build fake input with a stub read. `PromptInput` type has many fields; cast as never/unknown.\n\nTest asserts:\n- keys order = [\"persona\",\"verification_iron_law\",\"clarify_contract\",\"injection_guard\",\"current_project\",\"skills\",\"topics\"]\n- each render output === provider text for the same ctx (byte identity, same code path though).\n\nHmm, tautology again. But the real regression guard is: the section text = provider text (framework actually driving), plus provider tests assert exact constants. Combined, byte identity is pinned to constants. Good.\n\nAdditionally for the \"position\" assertion, the key order test is the important one.\n\nNow, one more issue: hoisting sections to module scope changes nothing semantically. The `render` imports remain.\n\n### Let me now check `resolvePersona` signature and `partnersStore` usage inside provider — passing function reference `partnersStore` matches `getStore: () => PartnersStore`.\n\n### Write code\n\nLet me start with injection.ts.\n\nCareful with existing exports: INJECTION_REGISTRY used by injection.test.ts and possibly elsewhere. I'll move the registry to `injection-registry.ts` and keep a re-export? Re-export would create a cycle (registry imports injection; injection re-exports registry → cycle). Avoid; update all references.\n\nLet me grep INJECTION_REGISTRY usage: only injection.ts and injection.test.ts. Good.\n\nNow write injection.ts changes."
      }
