      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now partner-context.ts rewrite. This is the trickiest. Plan:\n\n- Add imports: `collectInjections`, `INJECTION_ORDER`, `InjectionEntry`, `InjectionProvider` from injection.ts.\n- Remove `INJECTION_GUARD`/`injectionGuardEnabled` import? Guard provider removed → INJECTION_GUARD no longer used. But `injection-guard.ts` may be used elsewhere in this file? Only guard. Remove import.\n- Add `partnerContextProviders(partnerId, deps)` factory.\n- Keep `buildPartnerDisciplineSection(partnerId)` as a function that composes from the same constants — tests use it. Could implement it via `collectInjections(disciplineProviders(partnerId), ctx)` joined. But it's used independently; simpler keep it as-is (it's the source of truth for discipline text) and providers call it? No — we need individual segments for entry ids.\n\nApproach: define a function `disciplineBlocks(partnerId): Array<{id, text}>`, and `buildPartnerDisciplineSection` = blocks.map(text).join(\"\\n\\n\"). Providers use blocks.\n\nThen:\n```ts\nexport function partnerContextProviders(partnerId: string, deps: PartnerContextDeps = {}): InjectionProvider[] {\n  const store = deps.store ?? partnersStore();\n  // 懒取一次（多次 provider 调用只读一次库）\n  let currentLoaded = false;\n  let current: ReturnType<PartnersStore[\"currentVersion\"]> = null;\n  const currentOf = () => { if (!currentLoaded) { current = store.currentVersion(partnerId); currentLoaded = true; } return current; };\n  const contractText = () => renderContractSection(currentOf()?.contractSource ?? store.readContractFromHome(partnerId)) ?? undefined;\n  const goalText = () => buildPartnerGoalSection(partnerId, store);\n  const statusText = () => buildPartnerStatusSection(partnerId, conversationId, {...deps, store});\n  ...\n}\n```\nBut conversationId is needed for status; factory signature `(partnerId, conversationId, deps)`.\n\nProviders array order must be the discipline order interleaved? Entries have order constants, so the array order doesn't matter for collection (sorted). But keep declaration order logical.\n\nEach provider returns entry(id, text, order, \"message\", \"session\").\n\nReturn type `InjectionProvider[]`.\n\nThen buildPartnerTurnContext:\n```ts\nexport function buildPartnerTurnContext(partnerId, conversationId, deps = {}) {\n  const store = deps.store ?? partnersStore();\n  const current = store.currentVersion(partnerId);\n  const soul = current?.soulSource ?? store.readSoulFromHome(partnerId) ?? \"\";\n  const entries = collectInjections(partnerContextProviders(partnerId, conversationId, deps), { conversationId, partnerId }).message;\n  const byId = new Map(entries.map(e => [e.id, e.text]));\n  const contract = byId.get(PARTNER_CONTRACT_ID) ?? null;\n  const goal = byId.get(PARTNER_GOAL_ID) ?? null;\n  const status = byId.get(PARTNER_STATUS_ID) ?? null;\n  const discipline = DISCIPLINE_IDS.map(id=>byId.get(id)).filter(Boolean).join(\"\\n\\n\");\n  const text = entries.map(e=>e.text).join(\"\\n\\n\") || undefined;\n  return { soul, contract, goal, discipline, status, text };\n}\n```\nNote soul read twice (currentVersion twice) — minor. Could pass `current` via deps? Just accept.\n\nGuard removed: no `guard` field. Update interface.\n\nWait: `buildPartnerTurnContext` previously had `discipline` computed before status, and `text` = [contract, goal, discipline, status, guard]. With entries, text = sorted entries joined. Same order.\n\nNow `source`/ids: define exported consts:\n```ts\nexport const PARTNER_INJECTION_IDS = { contract: \"partner_contract\", ... }\n```\n\nAnd a registry provider:\n```ts\nexport const partnerContextInjectionProvider: InjectionProvider = (ctx) => {\n  if (!ctx.partnerId) return undefined;\n  const entries = collectInjections(partnerContextProviders(ctx.partnerId, Number(ctx.conversationId)), ctx).message;\n  return entries;\n};\n```\nThis returns entries already collected; audit collects again (safe).\n\nCareful: In dryRun, status provider would scan workRoot. To keep audit reasonable, status provider returns undefined when ctx.dryRun. But provider factory doesn't get ctx... Providers receive ctx at call time; so status provider can `(ctx) => ctx.dryRun ? undefined : ...`. But then buildPartnerTurnContext (live) passes ctx without dryRun → status included. Audit → omitted. Then audit's contract/goal/discipline show, status not. Document. Good compromise (avoids opening chancellor sqlite on a read endpoint).\n\nAlso `soul` isn't an entry.\n\nNow `guard` removal affects `PartnerTurnContext` interface and tests. Update tests to assert text ends with discipline? I'll adjust partner-context.test lines 277-329 and 306-320.\n\nLet me write the new partner-context sections. I'll read lines 378-458 again and rewrite that block."
      }
    ],
