ep audit reasonable, status provider returns undefined when ctx.dryRun. But provider factory doesn't get ctx... Providers receive ctx at call time; so status provider can `(ctx) => ctx.dryRun ? undefined : ...`. But then buildPartnerTurnContext (live) passes ctx without dryRun → status included. Audit → omitted. Then audit's contract/goal/discipline show, status not. Document. Good compromise (avoids opening chancellor sqlite on a read endpoint).\n\nAlso `soul` isn't an entry.\n\nNow `guard` removal affects `PartnerTurnContext` interface and tests. Update tests to assert text ends with discipline? I'll adjust partner-context.test lines 277-329 and 306-320.\n\nLet me write the new partner-context sections. I'll read lines 378-458 again and rewrite that block.",
