        "text": "Now rewrite the block from \"整体装配\" (line ~378) to the end. Let me construct replacement carefully, preserving buildPartnerDisciplineSection's exact output.\n\nI'll replace from `// ── 整体装配 ─────` to end of file.\n\nNew content:\n\n```ts\n// ── 整体装配 ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/** 纪律段（2026-11-10 批 12 + 批 16）... */\nfunction disciplineBlocks(partnerId: string): Array<{ id: string; text: string }> {\n  const blocks: Array<{ id: string; text: string | undefined }> = [\n    { id: \"partner_verification\", text: verificationIronLawFor(partnerId) },\n    { id: \"partner_ruling\", text: RULING_DISCIPLINE },\n    { id: \"partner_work_silence\", text: WORK_SILENCE_DISCIPLINE },\n    { id: \"partner_grounding\", text: GROUNDING_DISCIPLINE },\n    { id: \"partner_artifact_handoff\", text: artifactHandoffEnabled() ? ARTIFACT_HANDOFF : undefined },\n    { id: \"partner_owner_data\", text: ownerDataDisciplineEnabled() ? OWNER_DATA_DISCIPLINE : undefined },\n    { id: \"partner_brief_card\", text: partnerId === CHIEF_PARTNER_ID || !briefCardRulesEnabled() ? undefined : BRIEF_CARD_RULES },\n    { id: \"partner_attention\", text: ATTENTION_ONE_QUESTION },\n  ];\n  return blocks.filter((b): b is {id:string;text:string} => Boolean(b.text));\n}\n\nexport function buildPartnerDisciplineSection(partnerId: string): string {\n  return disciplineBlocks(partnerId).map(b => b.text).join(\"\\n\\n\");\n}\n```\n\nOrder constants mapping for discipline ids: `DISCIPLINE_ORDERS: Record<string, number>`.\n\nThen:\n```ts\nfunction contextEntry(id: string, text: string | undefined): InjectionEntry | undefined {\n  if (!text) return undefined;\n  return { id, text, order: ..., scope: \"session\", channel: \"message\" };\n}\n```\nNeed order lookup: a map from id → order. Build:\n```ts\nconst ORDER: Record<string, number> = {\n  partner_contract: INJECTION_ORDER.partner_contract,\n  ...\n};\n```\n\n`partnerContextProviders(partnerId, conversationId, deps)`:\n```ts\nexport function partnerContextProviders(\n  partnerId: string,\n  conversationId: number,\n  deps: PartnerContextDeps = {},\n): InjectionProvider[] {\n  const store = deps.store ?? partnersStore();\n  let current: ReturnType<PartnersStore[\"currentVersion\"]> | undefined;\n  const currentOf = () => (current === undefined ? (current = store.currentVersion(partnerId)) : current);\n  const entries: Array<() => InjectionEntry | undefined> = [\n    () => contextEntry(\"partner_contract\", renderContractSection(currentOf()?.contractSource ?? store.readContractFromHome(partnerId)), \"partner_contract\"),\n    () => contextEntry(\"partner_goal\", buildPartnerGoalSection(partnerId, store), ...),\n    ...disciplineBlocks(partnerId).map(b => () => contextEntry(b.id, b.text, b.id)),\n    (ctx) => ctx.dryRun ? undefined : contextEntry(\"partner_status\", buildPartnerStatusSection(partnerId, conversationId, {...deps, store}), \"partner_status\"),\n  ];\n  return entries.map(fn => (ctx) => fn(ctx));\n}\n```\nHmm, type: provider takes ctx. Simplify: return array of `(ctx) => ...`.\n\nNote `currentOf` memo returns `undefined` if not found; but `current === undefined` sentinel conflates \"not loaded\" with \"loaded undefined\". Use a flag.\n\n`contextEntry` signature with order id.\n\nThen `buildPartnerTurnContext` as described.\n\nRegistry provider:\n```ts\nexport const partnerContextProvider: InjectionProvider = (ctx) => {\n  if (!ctx.partnerId) return undefined;\n  return collectInjections(\n    partnerContextProviders(ctx.partnerId, Number(ctx.conversationId)),\n    ctx,\n  ).message;\n};\n```\n\nCareful: in `partnerContextProviders`, status provider uses conversationId captured from arg, not ctx. Fine.\n\nDedupe within partner collection: ids unique.\n\nGuard removal: `PartnerTurnContext` loses `guard`. Update interface + comments.\n\nLet me write the replacement."
