        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now lifecycle.ts: hoist sections to a module-level constant and delegate renders; rewrite beforeRequest message injections.\n\nFirst, sections. Replace the inline `sections: [...]` array with `sections: LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS`. Define `LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS` above openHarness.\n\nRenders:\n\n```ts\nexport const LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS: readonly PromptSection[] = [\n  {\n    key: \"persona\",\n    render: async (input) => {\n      const conversationId = Number(input.conversationId);\n      const partnerId = partnerIdOfSession(conversationId);\n      const kinds = await input.read.snapshot(ChatKinds, CTX);\n      const chatKind = kinds?.byInternal?.[String(input.conversationId)] === \"worker\" ? \"worker\" : \"chief\";\n      return collectInjections([personaProvider], { conversationId, partnerId, chatKind }).system[0]?.text;\n    },\n  },\n  ...\n];\n```\n\nWait: persona's original early-return before snapshot for non-chief partner. If I always snapshot, behavior change (read only). I said acceptable, but let me avoid it cheaply: in persona render, early return if `isNonChiefPartner(partnerId)`? The provider also checks. I can export the predicate from lifecycle-injections. Hmm, but then render duplicates the gate. Use provider-only and accept the snapshot. For topics, the original also checks TOPICS_ENABLED before anything — trivial. For clarify, switch check first.\n\nI'll keep renders minimal (resolve facts → collect), letting providers gate. This guarantees single source of gating logic; the only cost is extra snapshot reads for sessions that would have skipped. Let me quantify: non-chief partner sessions: persona no longer skips snapshot (1 read). clarify no longer skips snapshot (1 read, only when switch on). topics: snapshot now happens even for group/non-chief partner (1 read). These are `harness.snapshot(ChatKinds)` — a LiveDoc read from in-memory/durable, cheap. Content unchanged. Acceptable; I'll note in change record \"每 render 取一次种类快照（原先分流后才取），仅多一次只读快照，不改变注入内容\".\n\nNeed helpers to resolve partnerId / group:\n\n```ts\nfunction partnerOfSession(conversationId: number): string | null {\n  if (!COMPANIONS_ENABLED) return null;\n  try { return partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession(conversationId); } catch { return null; }\n}\nfunction isGroupConversation(conversationId: number): boolean {\n  if (!COMPANIONS_ENABLED) return false;\n  try { return partnersStore().isGroupSession(conversationId); } catch { return false; }\n}\n```\nThese mirror original try/catch semantics (\"档案库读失败按总管处理\").\n\nThen each render:\n\npersona: partnerId + chatKind → collect.\nverification: partnerId → collect.\nclarify: partnerId + chatKind → collect (provider checks switch).\nguard: unchanged.\ncurrent_project: collect([currentProjectProvider], {conversationId}).\nskills: collect.\ntopics: partnerId + group + chatKind → collect.\n\nKeys unchanged; order unchanged.\n\nNow beforeRequest. Replace the memory/slash/recover pushes with collected entries at the end. Need `used` before collect. Rewrite the hook body:\n\n```ts\nbeforeRequest: async (request, api, ctx) => {\n  const lastUser = [...request.messages].reverse().find((m) => m.role === \"user\");\n  const userText = lastUser ? contentText(lastUser.content) : \"\";\n\n  // (used calc / relay begin / limit state) ...\n\n  // 5 处消息注入：框架统一收集 → 按原顺序压入\n  const messageCtx: InjectionContext = {\n    conversationId: api.conversationId,\n    partnerId: partnerOfSession(api.conversationId),\n    turn: used,\n    userText,\n  };\n  const extra = collectInjections(LIFECYCLE_MESSAGE_PROVIDERS, messageCtx).message.map((item) => ({\n    role: \"system\" as const,\n    content: item.text,\n    timestamp: Date.now(),\n  }));\n\n  if (extra.length === 0) return undefined;\n  return { messages: [...extra, ...request.messages] };\n}\n```\n\nBut the original pushed memory/slash/recover BEFORE computing `used` and had side effects in between; order of side effects: takeRecoverNote (now via provider at collect), beginRelayRun, claimRelayTarget, toolsBlocked... collect happens after. The recover note consumption order relative to `used` doesn't matter.\n\nHowever: `turnLimitProvider` needs `MAX_TURNS` condition; also the code adds `toolsBlocked`, `limitHits`, warning, abort — keep in the hook.\n\nBut careful: original `else if (used === 1)` resets toolsBlocked. Keep.\n\nAlso `partnerContextProvider` uses ctx.partnerId — I'll pass partnerId resolved (with try/catch semantics). But the original try/catch around partner resolution logs \"[partner] 会话 N 上下文装配失败\" on store error. If my helper swallows the error (returns null), no log. Minor difference in logging only. To preserve, pass `partnerId` only when resolvable? Simpler: in messageCtx, don't set partnerId; let the provider resolve within its try/catch (as written: `ctx.partnerId ?? partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession()`). But `partnerOfSession` returns null on error → `?? ` won't trigger because null is not undefined... In the provider I used `ctx.partnerId ?? ...`; if ctx.partnerId is null, `??` returns `partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession(...)` — actually null ?? x → x. Yes! `??` only falls through on null/undefined. So if I set partnerId: null, provider will query the store itself inside its try. Good — error logged as before.\n\nSo messageCtx: `{ conversationId, turn: used, userText }` (no partnerId) → partner provider resolves internally. \n\nBut `memoryRecallProvider` uses conversationId → recallContext. Good.\n\nNow section renders need partnerId for gating; resolve there.\n\nNow `extra` timestamps: original each push had its own Date.now() at push time; now all at map time (same ms likely). Byte-identical content; timestamps aren't part of prompt bytes? They are part of the message object (`timestamp`) maybe used by durable. The original timestamps differ by microseconds across pushes; not meaningful. Fine.\n\nWait — important: original memory push happened BEFORE `used` computation but the message array is prepended in `extra` order. New order: same list order. OK.\n\nAnother subtlety: original computed `memory` and pushed it even if `MAX_TURNS` hit; yes.\n\nNow `LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS` typing: import `PromptSection` type from pi-durable. `sections: LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS`.\n\nLet me now edit lifecycle.ts. First imports: add `PromptSection` type; import collectInjections (already), guardProvider (already), and the new providers.\n\nRemove now-unused imports after refactor: `TOPICS_ENABLED, topicsStore` (topics moved), `wrapUntrustedObjective`, `skillSlashOf`, `clarifyContractEnabled, clarifyContractFor` (moved), `PERSONA, WORKER_PERSONA`? persona moved; `VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW, lifecycleOwnsVerification` moved; `currentProject, currentProjectEnabled`? currentProject still used by sessionCwd/currentProject in shared; lifecycle imports `currentProject` for... let me check usage in lifecycle: line 158 imports currentProject; used at line 566 in current_project render only. So remove. `partnersStore, CHIEF_PARTNER_ID` still used elsewhere (relay etc.) — keep. `COMPANIONS_ENABLED` used in beforeTool/relay etc. `resolvePersona` only persona → remove. `recallContext` only memory → remove. `skillStore` still used for slash? moved to provider; but lifecycle uses skillStore elsewhere? line 141 imports; used at 989 (slash) and 581 (skills). Both moved → remove. `TURN_LIMIT_INSTRUCTION, MAX_TURNS` still used in hook logic (MAX_TURNS yes; TURN_LIMIT_INSTRUCTION moved → remove). `takeRecoverNote` moved → remove. `wrapUntrustedObjective` moved → remove. `workSummaryFor` moved → remove. `buildPartnerTurnContext` moved → remove.\n\nCareful: `currentProject` import from shared also used by `sessionCwd`? No, shared defines it. lifecycle imports `currentProject` and `currentProjectEnabled` from projects.ts and shared.ts respectively? Line 113: `import { currentProjectEnabled, projectsStore, workspaceRootReal } from \"../projects.ts\";` and line 158 `currentProject` from shared.ts. Remove both `currentProject` and `currentProjectEnabled` if unused. Used in beforeTool? projectsStore/workspaceRootReal used in path guard. OK.\n\nLet me do the edits step by step with grep verification after.\n\nFirst replace the sections array block (lines 492-636)."
      }
    ],
