        "text": "APP_SKILLS_DIR is the repo's `apps/server/skills/` which has built-in skills! So even with AGENT_SKILLS_DIR temp, app dir is in the chain → skillStore has built-in skills. That's fine and deterministic — and useful for testing skills/slash. But the app skills change over time; tests should not hardcode names. I can read `skillStore.names()[0]` in tests.\n\nHowever, skill visibility: `skillVisible` = skillStateEnabled() && getSkillState().isEnabled(name). Default state likely all disabled unless configured. Let me check skill-state defaults; tests import skillStore and indexFor may return undefined when all invisible. For the test, I can assert provider === skillStore.indexFor(id) (identity), and for slash, use a skill only if manual available.\n\nSimplify tests: skillsProvider live must equal `skillStore?.indexFor(id)`; and dryRun must be undefined. That proves the provider takes frozen index without re-implementing. Plus a freeze test: call provider twice → same text; change nothing. Hmm.\n\nOK let me now write the new injection.test.ts comprehensively.\n\nTest list:\nFramework (keep existing):\n1. collect sort/dedupe/channel (keep).\n2. context shape? skip.\n3. guard byte-identity + audit no text.\n4. audit switch.\nNew:\nB:\n5. LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS keys order snapshot (position).\n6. persona provider: chief → PERSONA (no chief record since temp store), worker → WORKER_PERSONA; partner non-chief → undefined.\n   But COMPANIONS_ENABLED default true; partnersStore() uses temp DB. resolvePersona → chiefPartnerEnabled? default true → store.get(\"chief\") null → fallback PERSONA. Good.\n7. verification: null → VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW; \"partner-x\" → undefined.\n8. clarify: default → CLARIFY_CONTRACT; worker → undefined; partner-x → undefined; AGENT_CLARIFY_CONTRACT=false → undefined.\n9. current_project: currentProjectEnabled default true; projectsStore() reads temp? Need PROJECTS_DB_PATH env; check projects.ts default path. If not set, it may touch .data. Let me check.\n10. skills: live == skillStore.indexFor; dryRun undefined.\n11. topics: exact text \"在跟的课题：（暂无）\\n\\n课题嗅探…\"; with dryRun and a pending push? Creating a topic requires store API. Maybe skip push; assert drain semantics via `topicsStore().create(...)`? Let me check API for creating topics with pendingPush — complex. Instead assert no-side-effect: dryRun doesn't throw and text equals non-dryRun text when no pending.\nC:\n12. memoryRecall: MEMORY_ENABLED=false → undefined (byte? not meaningful). Could enable memory with temp DB? MEMORY_DB_PATH temp + MEMORY_ENABLED unset → creates engine and recall \"\". Better: assert provider text === recallContext(id, text) exactly (both empty). Weak. I'll assert undefined when no engine and that assistant provider id/order/channel shape.\n13. partner discipline segments: build context; assert text = contract + goal + discipline + status joined; assert segment ids/orders; assert no guard; assert chief has no verification segment.\nD:\n14. message provider order: collect LIFECYCLE_MESSAGE_PROVIDERS with turn=MAX_TURNS+1 & userText=\"\" → ids [\"turn_limit\"]; with turn=1 and no partner → [].\n15. recoverNote: markRecoverResume(id) → provider returns takeRecoverNote text; second call undefined; dryRun doesn't consume.\n16. skillSlash: with a fake skill? skillStore is real. Could skip if no slashable skill; instead test the *template* by stubbing? Providers use the module-level skillStore, not injectable. Hmm. Test: if skillStore has names, take names[0], get manual; if manual, assert provider text === template. If not, skip (assert undefined for unknown name). Use `test(\"...\", {skip: !name})`? Node test supports `t.skip()`. Simpler: assert provider({userText:\"/__no_such_skill__\"}) === undefined, and if a manual exists, assert exact template. Conditional assertions are okay.\n17. partnerContextProvider: needs DB with partner; use PartnersStore temp + link session, build via buildPartnerTurnContext and compare text; provider returns entry text === turnContext.text. But provider uses `partnersStore()` singleton (temp env), and deps workSummary real → workSummaryFor reads work DB (may touch .data!). workSummaryFor injected in the provider. Hmm — calling partnerContextProvider in test would call workSummaryFor → opens work-record DB (probably .data). To avoid, don't test provider directly; test buildPartnerTurnContext with deps (workSummary stub) — that's the same assembly.\n\n18. audit registry: with ctx {conversationId:1, chatKind:\"chief\", partnerId:null, dryRun:true} → sources include lifecycle & assist; no text; ids list contains persona, verification_iron_law, clarify_contract, injection_guard, current_project, topics (skills skipped); partner-context absent; memory absent.\n19. order snapshot: INJECTION_ORDER sorted list frozen.\n\n20. Dedupe/merge: partner text has no 【材料安全】 (done in partner-context.test) + guard section still returns it (guard test).\n\nNeed to know projects store path env. Check."
