        "text": "`skillVisible` implementation in assist: `skillStateEnabled() && getSkillState().isEnabled(name)`. If SKILL_STATE=false, `skillStateEnabled()` false → visible false. That looks inverted vs the comment (\"false 一行 = 回到全开\"), but maybe `visible` has inverted semantics? In skills.ts `.filter(visible)` — visible=true keeps. So SKILL_STATE=false → nothing kept. This is a pre-existing inconsistency (not my task). I'll avoid relying on skills content in tests.\n\nTo test skills provider meaningfully without real skills: I can't inject a store. Test identity with `skillStore?.indexFor` and dryRun undefined. If skillStore is null (no skills at all), `skillStore?.indexFor` is undefined and provider undefined — tautological but shows no crash. Fine; the real guarantee is the section render calls the provider (test via LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS).\n\nWait, actually I can enable a skill via `AGENT_SKILLS_STATE_PATH` temp file with `{\"enabled\":{\"<name>\":true}}` for a name I create in AGENT_SKILLS_DIR. Let me check skill file format: line 1 = summary? Read scanSkillDir."
