        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Easy: write `<tmp>/skills/probe-skill.md` with first line a summary and body. Then set `AGENT_SKILLS_STATE_PATH` to a temp json with `{\"enabled\":{\"probe-skill\":true}}` BEFORE import (getSkillState lazily reads at first call, so setting env before first skillVisible call is enough; but skillStatePath resolves env at creation. Fine, set before import).\n\nBut careful: skillStore is created at import of assist, which calls `createSkillStore(..., {visible: skillVisible})` — the visible function reads state lazily at render time. Good.\n\nThen skillsProvider live returns the index text containing \"probe-skill\". Slash provider returns the template with manual body.\n\nNow write the new injection.test.ts. It'll be sizable. Let me write it.\n\nNote: dynamic imports after setting env, because assist's memoryEngine/skillStore are module-level. Use `await import`.\n\nAlso top-level test file uses `before/after` for guard env. I'll just delete AGENT_INJECTION_GUARD before importing.\n\nOrder snapshot: freeze full sorted array.\n\nLet me write carefully, importing types via `import type`.\n\nFor partner context test in this file, use `buildPartnerTurnContext` from partner-context with a temp PartnersStore and deps stubs.\n\nTest of LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS renders: fake input needs `read.snapshot` returning `{byInternal:{}}` and conversationId 1. Render signature has 2 args; call `section.render(input as never, CTX as never)`. `CTX` from shared? import from \"./shared.ts\" triggers apps imports? shared imports projects only. Fine. Or pass `{} as never`.\n\nFor persona render with conversationId 1: partnerOfSession(1) → partnersStore() temp DB → null; snapshot {} → chief; provider → resolvePersona(partnersStore, PERSONA) → chiefPartnerEnabled default? Let me check `chiefPartnerEnabled`. If default true, store.get(\"chief\") on temp DB → null → fallback PERSONA. Good.\n\nFor current_project render: projectsStore temp DB, no current project → \"当前无特定项目（杂事模式）。文件操作默认在主工作区。\".\n\nFor topics render: TOPICS_ENABLED default? `TOPICS_ENABLED` computed at import: check default true. With TOPICS_STATE_PATH temp (no file) → digest \"\" → text \"在跟的课题：（暂无）\\n\\n课题嗅探…\". Good.\n\nskills render: with probe skill enabled and temp skills dir, returns index text. This doubles as the byte-identity golden:\n```\n\"可用技能（对方的事需要按某个流程引导时，先调 skill(name) 取完整手册再开始）：\\n- probe-skill：<summary>\"\n```\n\nNow let's write the file.\n\nAlso keep framework tests (collect sorting/dedupe/channel/audit switch) — rewrite them to use new API.\n\nRegarding `auditInjections(INJECTION_REGISTRY, ctx)` in tests: importing the registry imports all provider modules including assist (already imported) and partner-context (imports chancellor store). Fine.\n\nAudit ctx: `{conversationId: 1, chatKind:\"chief\", partnerId:null, dryRun:true}`. Expect ids:\n- persona, verification_iron_law, clarify_contract, injection_guard, current_project, topics (skills: dryRun → undefined)\n- assist memory (userText undefined → \"\" → undefined), task_memory (dryRun → undefined)\n- partner (no partnerId → undefined)\nSo 6 rows. Sources lifecycle only. That doesn't demonstrate assist/partner sources. I could call `auditInjections` with a partnerId and check partner rows appear (contract/goal/discipline). For that, need partner in temp store + session link. Then audit ctx partnerId = that id, conversationId = linked id, dryRun true → contract? partner created with template contract → renderContractSection(template) non-empty. goal null. discipline 7 (non-chief: verification + ruling + ... + brief card + attention = 8) and status skipped. So partner rows appear.\n\nAlso `assist` source in audit: memory provider needs `userText` — with MEMORY_ENABLED=false, recallContext returns \"\" even with text. So no assist row. task_memory dryRun → undefined. So assist never appears in audit. Hmm, requirement 4.2 \"source 能区分来源模块\" — the field exists and lifecycle/assist rows carry it, but assist rows only when memory enabled. For the http probe, memory enabled? The probe server likely has memory enabled by default (MEMORY_ENABLED not set) and userText empty → recall \"\" → no row. So assist won't show. That's fine—source field is per-row and correct.\n\nCould I make memory provider return an entry even when empty? No (would change behavior).\n\nTest assist source: is there a way to get an assist row in audit? task_memory would be non-empty if diary has entries and dryRun false. In audit we set dryRun true. Could allow taskMemoryProvider in dryRun if text computable without writes? taskMemoryBlock writes (syncDiaryToMemory). We could pass dryRun to taskMemoryBlock? No.\n\nSo assist rows are unreachable in audit by design (memory needs a live user text; task memory needs writes). Hmm, that weakens 4.2. But `source` still distinguishes when present in principle. I'll document: 审计列出可静态判定的注入；assist 的两条需要轮次正文/任务通道，不在会话审计里出现。Hmm, the task says \"审计端点现在能列出全部注入条目\" — risk.\n\nAlternative: make audit include *message* providers with an empty userText? memory returns undefined because recallContext(\"\") returns \"\". Can't fix.\n\nHmm, maybe audit's purpose is listing entries, and message ones can't be enumerated without a turn. I'll document this boundary honestly as \"已知边界\" and note it in the change record. The endpoint still lists all *system-side* and partner segments.\n\nWait — maybe I can improve: audit ctx could include `userText: \"\"`, and providers for message type could still be listed with `length: 0`? No, don't fabricate.\n\nOK proceed.\n\nOne more: `source` for the 5 lifecycle message providers: registered individually (skill_slash, recover_note, turn_limit) but not partner_context aggregate. Registering them means audit could show `turn_limit` if ctx.turn > MAX_TURNS (audit has no turn → no). Fine.\n\nLet me write the test file now."
      }
    ],
