        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "I wrote some garbage lines (`const { scoreTrip } = { scoreTrip: null };`, `_MAX_TURNS`, import recoverNoteProvider after use — `const` TDZ issue: the test callback runs later, but the `const { recoverNoteProvider }` declaration after tests is fine at runtime since tests run after module eval. But tsconfig may complain about use before declaration? TS allows referencing a const declared later inside a function body (no error unless called immediately). Still messy.\n\nAlso `entryOf` returns `.system[0]` but message providers need `.message`. I used entryOf only for system. For message entries I access provider directly.\n\nWait `entryOf(turnLimitProvider)` not used; fine.\n\nAlso `entryOf(guardProvider)` type: `collectInjections([provider as never], ...)`.\n\nLet me clean the file: remove scoreTrip junk, move the recoverNoteProvider import up, remove _MAX_TURNS hack.\n\nAlso `import { VERIFICATION_IRON_LAW } from \"./agent/turn-gate.ts\"` — wrong path? injection.test.ts is in src/agent/, so turn-gate is \"./turn-gate.ts\". I wrote \"./agent/turn-gate.ts\" — wrong. Same for delegation (\"./delegation.ts\" → \"../delegation.ts\"). And recover-note is \"./recover-note.ts\".\n\nLet me fix all import paths:\n- `./turn-gate.ts`\n- `../delegation.ts`\n- `./recover-note.ts`\n- assist: \"./assist.ts\"\n- others fine.\n\nAlso `MAX_TURNS` import duplicated. Consolidate.\n\nAlso `LIFECYCLE_SECTIONS` import triggers lifecycle.ts import → heavy (pi-durable, tools). Acceptable? It also imports `openai-compat`? No. It imports createTools etc. Might be slow but fine. However importing lifecycle.ts imports `./assist.ts` etc. Fine.\n\nHmm, importing lifecycle.ts in a unit test could have side effects: `setApprovalLevelSource`, no server start. It imports `approvals.ts` etc. Probably okay (other tests import partner-context which imports chancellor).\n\nLet me rewrite the header portion cleanly."
      }
    ],
