    "rawContent": [
      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Two failures:\n1. partner rows missing — because `partnerContextInjectionProvider` uses `partnersStore()` singleton (default temp path from env = partner.sqlite), not the partner3 store. The partner was created in partner3.sqlite. So audit's provider sees no partner. Fix test: create the partner in the singleton store (the env-configured one) instead of a separate DB. Use `partnersStore()` import.\n\nBut the singleton Partner store was possibly already created by earlier tests (persona etc.) pointing at root/partners.sqlite. I can import `partnersStore` and create partner there. Then audit provider will find it.\n\n2. EPERM removing temp dir on Windows — because PartnerStore/DB handles remain open (singleton). Just don't rmSync the root at after; or wrap in try/catch. Simplest: try/catch ignore. Tests elsewhere likely do rmSync after closing; our singletons can't close. Use `rmSync(..., {force:true})` still EPERM. Ignore errors.\n\nAlso check `partner_contract` may render undefined if the partner created without contract? `store.create` writes CONTRACT.md template and version with contractSource? In partner-context test, create → currentVersion contract = template (asserted). So non-empty.\n\nBut `renderContractSection` requires `partnerContractEnabled()` true (default). Good.\n\nFix both."
      }
    ],
