        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Http probe passes. Let me confirm the §4.5 lines specifically (tail cut them out). Search output? Rerun grep. But \"端到端全部通过\" means all checks passed including 4.5.\n\nNow: potential runtime issue — `partnerContextProvider` in lifecycle-injections imports buildPartnerTurnContext, which now returns text without guard. That's the merge. Also the provider resolves partnerId via `ctx.partnerId ?? partnersStore()...`; in lifecycle ctx has no partnerId → resolves inside try. Good.\n\nBut wait: original partner context block was gated on `used === 1 && COMPANIONS_ENABLED` and resolved partnerId; if `partnerIdOfSession` throws, catch logs. My provider is registered in LIFECYCLE_MESSAGE_PROVIDERS and is called on every collect (every request), returning early if turn !== 1. Good.\n\nOne important semantic check: original memory/slash/recover pushes happened *before* `used` was computed. Now `collect` happens after the turn-limit block. `takeRecoverNote` consumer order relative to nothing else. Fine.\n\nBUT: `MARK_RECOVER_RESUME` is set in afterTool; if the run hits the turn limit, original still pushed the note plus turn-limit. Now both are in the same collection, sorted by order → recover(120) before turn_limit(130). Same as original. Good.\n\nAnother important check: `extra.length === 0` early return — same.\n\nNow, `auditInjections` in the http endpoint calls `openChat` which creates a Harness on first audit call. The probe passed.\n\nNext: `pnpm probe` (kernel semantics) — AGENTS says run per change scope. We changed beforeRequest/extra push; `pnpm probe` is the kernel semantics probe. Task requires typecheck/test/http only, but AGENTS table says kernel semantics → pnpm probe. Let me run it to be safe (it's \"真起服务 + 真 HTTP\"). Check root package scripts."
      }
