returns \"partner\" for partner sessions; I map `=== \"worker\" ? worker : chief`. So chief for partner sessions, and persona provider checks partnerId first → undefined for non-chief. Good.\n\n11. **`partnerContextProvider` catch message**: identical.\n\n12. **Ordering of `extra`**: collect sorts by order; memory 100 < skill_slash 110 < recover 120 < turn_limit 130 < partner 140. Original push order memory, slash, recover, turnLimit, partner. Same.\n\n13. **`extra` array construction moved after turn-limit**: The original pushed memory/slash/recover *before* `api.snapshot(LiveDoc)` — any chance `takeRecoverNote` and `recallContext` readings differ if run state changes? No.\n\n14. **`TURN_LIMIT_INSTRUCTION` removal from lifecycle imports**: used only in provider now. Typecheck passed.\n\n15. **`process.env.AGENT_INJECTION_GUARD` tests**: `entryOf(guardProvider)` relies on guard enabled; we deleted env at module top. But other test files run in separate processes, so fine.\n\n16. **Injection audit shape changed** (added channel) — docs need update (接口文档 §? maybe describes endpoint). Let me check docs for the endpoint description; task says update 变更记录 only, but AGENTS says contract changes → 接口文档.md. The endpoint row shape changed → must update 接口文档.md. Let me grep."
