        "text": "`taskMemoryBlock` still exported via agent.ts and used only in memory-ingest comment. Keep the export (public API used by tasks/openai-compat historically; removing would be unrelated refactor). Fine.\n\n`.zb/` untracked — not mine (likely tool artifacts). Ignore.\n\nTask book file is untracked but was provided (I didn't create it). Fine.\n\nNow let me double-check a critical semantic: `LIFECYCLE_MESSAGE_PROVIDERS` includes `memoryRecallProvider` imported from assist. In lifecycle-injections I import `memoryRecallProvider` from \"./assist.ts\" — yes.\n\nAnother critical thing: in `beforeRequest`, I removed the explicit `memory`/`slash`/`recover` pushes but the `lastUser`/`contentText` are still used for userText. Good.\n\nBut wait: `partnerContextProvider` is in the message collection and is called on *every* model request (turn !== 1 returns undefined). Fine.\n\nPotential subtle bug: `partnerContextProvider` calls `partnersStore().partnerIdOfSession` when `ctx.partnerId` is undefined; but in lifecycle we don't pass partnerId, so every request (used>1) it short-circuits before that on `ctx.turn !== 1`. Good.\n\nNow: `collectInjections` sorts and dedupes. With one provider returning entries, dedupe by id. For 5 providers, ids unique. Good.\n\nBut `skillSlashProvider` uses `skillStore?.manual(name)` — for a disabled skill returns undefined → no injection (same as before).\n\nNow, a correctness check on `topicsProvider`: original checked `TOPICS_ENABLED` then group/partner then snapshot. Now render does snapshot always; provider checks. Content same. But `drainPendingPushes` now happens inside collect for the section — same place (render time). Good.\n\nOne more: original persona render returned `WORKER_PERSONA` for worker even if partnerId is chief; provider checks partner first (non-chief → undefined) then worker. Same.\n\nNow run full test + typecheck again, then http (already passed but index.ts unchanged since? I changed index.ts before probe run — yes probe run was after index change. Actually probe ran after index change? Order: I edited index.ts (audit + import), then ran typecheck, tests, then probe. Yes probe includes it.)\n\nWait: probe ran *before* I edited the probe? No: I edited probe then ran it. Good.\n\nBut I edited `injection.test.ts` after the full test run. Run full tests again to be safe. Also re-run typecheck (test edits)."
