        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "All green. Now let me do a self-review of the diff for quality issues:\n\n1. `lifecycle-injections.ts` — `entry` helper with unused param defaults? `scope` default \"session\". Used with \"turn\"/\"once\". Fine.\n2. `isNonChiefPartner` duplicated with `lifecycleOwnsVerification` semantics — fine.\n3. `partner-context.ts` — `ORDER` map and `entry` function; unused import `INJECTION_GUARD` removed. Check there's no leftover `injectionGuardEnabled` usage. Typecheck passed, so no.\n4. `injection.ts` — `InjectionScope` \"session\" etc. `INJECTION_GUARD_ID` still exported but unused? It's used only in injection.ts? grep. Probably unused now; it was used in batch A tests. Keeping exported constant is fine (public).\n5. `http-probe` — `injRow` typed `Record<string, unknown>`; `.source` access ok.\n\nLet me quickly review the final lifecycle section block to ensure comments aren't misleading and the code is clean. Also check that `chatKind` computation duplication is acceptable (3 copies). Could extract a helper to reduce duplication — but helper needs `input.read` typed; a small local async helper would be cleaner:\n\n```ts\nasync function kindOf(input, conversationId): Promise<\"chief\"|\"worker\"> {\n  const kinds = await input.read.snapshot(ChatKinds, CTX);\n  return kinds?.byInternal?.[String(input.conversationId)] === \"worker\" ? \"worker\" : \"chief\";\n}\n```\nType: `input` shape `{ conversationId: string|number; read: { snapshot: (...) } }` is awkward. Could type as `PromptInput`? `PromptInput` is exported from pi-durable types? It's used in PromptSection signature. I can type the helper param as `Parameters<NonNullable<PromptSection[\"render\"]>>[0]`. That works and is clean.\n\nLet me refactor to reduce the three copies:\n\n```ts\ntype SectionInput = Parameters<NonNullable<PromptSection[\"render\"]>>[0];\n\nasync function chatKindOfSection(input: SectionInput): Promise<\"chief\" | \"worker\"> {\n  const kinds = await input.read.snapshot(ChatKinds, CTX);\n  return kinds?.byInternal?.[String(input.conversationId)] === \"worker\" ? \"worker\" : \"chief\";\n}\n```\n\nThen renders use `const chatKind = await chatKindOfSection(input);`.\n\nThis is a small readability improvement, in scope. Do it.\n\nAlso `partnerOfSession`/`groupOfSession` fine.\n\nLet me apply."
      }
