        "text": "durable probe output has \"全部通过\"? grep only showed thinking. Since it's `&&`-chained and thinking ran, durable exited 0. Good.\n\nNow final self-review of remaining risks:\n\n1. `partner-context.ts`: `partnerContextInjectionProvider` calls `collectInjections(partnerContextProviders(...), ctx).message`. The status provider receives ctx (with dryRun true) → skipped. Contract/goal/discipline providers ignore ctx. Good.\n\n2. The `partnerContextProviders` closure `currentOf()` is called by contract provider only. Goal provider calls store.get. Discipline providers call partnerId-dependent functions. Fine.\n\n3. `buildPartnerTurnContext` calls `store.currentVersion` then collect → contract provider calls `currentOf()` which calls `store.currentVersion` again (second read). Minor duplicate read per turn. Could pass current to avoid; but it's one extra point query per turn — acceptable? The original did one read. Now two. Not a content change. Hmm, I could give `partnerContextProviders` an optional `current` param to reuse. But `buildPartnerTurnContext` calls it after reading current... Let me optimize minimally by allowing deps to carry a preloaded version? Over-engineering. Leave; note? Not worth noting.\n\nActually, cleaner: `buildPartnerTurnContext` currently reads `current` only for `soul`; the contract provider re-reads. I can remove the `soul` read duplication by having the provider... no, soul isn't an entry. Two reads per turn is fine.\n\n4. `injection.ts` doc says batch A only guard — updated header. Good.\n\n5. `INJECTION_GUARD_ID` still used? grep quickly.\n\n6. Does `injection-registry.ts` include the lifecycle `partner_context` provider? No — intentionally, because partner-context module provides segments. But then the *live* aggregate entry id `partner_context` is never in the registry. Fine. However the registry lacks a row for \"lifecycle's 5th extra.push\" — documented with comment.\n\n7. Requirement 4.2 source distinguishes `settled` — settled has no injection; documented.\n\n8. The audit endpoint resolves `openChat` which, on an unknown conversation, returns null (it may create? No: with externalId non-empty it looks up; returns null if not found). Good.\n\n9. `chatKindOf(chat)` returns \"partner\" for partner sessions; we map to chief. persona is then gated by partnerId → undefined. verify: `verificationIronLawProvider` uses partnerId. clarify uses partnerId. Good.\n\n10. Security: audit requires auth? The endpoint is under the app with auth middleware presumably. Not changed.\n\n11. `InjectionContext.dryRun` used by skills/topics/recover/taskMemory/status. Good.\n\nNow check git status and do a final read of the change record claim \"711 全绿\" — yes.\n\nOne more: the task says \"变更记录 ... 列出发现重复的注入\". Done.\n\nAlso \"最后回复：做了什么 / 每期验了什么 / 发现哪些重复 / 已知边界，控制在 600 字内\". Need ≤600 Chinese characters. Keep tight.\n\nBefore final, let me check that no debug leftovers in injection.test (e.g., unused import `PartnersStore` still used in the partner-context test — yes line with `new PartnersStore`). `mkdtempSync` etc used. Typecheck passed so no unused-var errors (noUnusedLocals may be off). Fine.\n\nLet me grep for `scoreTrip` leftovers (removed) and `console.log` added? None.\n\nCheck git status for unexpected files."
